    "title": "Birmingham police make arrest in connection to June homicide - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By M.K. Bryant ,\n5 hours ago\nBIRMINGHAM, Ala. ( WIAT ) -- The Birmingham Police Department has arrested a suspect in connection to a fatal shooting that occurred in June .\nThe incident occurred on June 18 at an apartment in the 800 block of 6th Street West. Police found 42-year-old Cornelius Parker suffering from a gunshot wound at the scene. Parker was taken to UAB Hospital for treatment, where he later died from his injuries.\nThe BPD reported that 28-year-old Jaylond Adams has been arrested for Capital Murder and 1st Degree Robbery in connection to the shooting. Adams was taken into custody on Thursday, Oct. 22, in the 400 block of Green Springs Highway. He will be taken to the Jefferson County Jail and held without bond.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Alabama's 42.\n2",
    "summary": "The incident occurred on June 18 at an apartment in the 800 block of 6th Street West. Police found 42-year-old Cornelius Parker suffering from a gunshot wound at the scene. The BPD reported that 28-year-old Jaylond Adams has been arrested for Capital Murder and 1st Degree Robbery in connection to the shooting. Adams was taken into custody on Thursday, Oct. 22, in the 400 block of Green Springs Highway. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Alabama's 42.",
